course: dictionary
lesson: 3102
title: Eightfold: eight times, or eight parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Eightfold is made from eight and a word ending that adds the idea of times. It has two main meanings: eight times as much, or having eight parts. Look at the sentence around it to choose. «The price rose eightfold.» Price is about money, so eightfold means the price grew to eight times as much.
explain: Clues decide the meaning. If you see a number, a sum or the word «increase», think eight times as much. If you see parts, ways or a list, think eight parts. In religion, «the Eightfold Path» names a set of eight parts, not a sum.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The Eightfold Path leads there» makes sense with «eight ways to live well», but not with «eight times as much path». Always test your idea before you trust it.
fact: Eightfold means eight times as much or as many, as in «The price rose eightfold.»
fact: In maths, eightfold means multiply by 8: if 5 grows eightfold, it becomes 40.
fact: Eightfold can also mean having eight parts.
fact: The Noble Eightfold Path is the Buddha's teaching of eight ways to live well: right view, right intention, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness and right concentration.
fact: In religion lessons, the Eightfold Path is shown as a wheel with eight spokes, and Buddhists believe it is how suffering can end.
exercise: «The price rose eightfold.» What does eightfold mean here? | *Eight times as much | Eight more than before | Half as much | Eight coins
exercise: In maths, if 5 grows eightfold, what is the new number? | 13 | 8 | 58 | *40
exercise: What does the Noble Eightfold Path have? | Four parts | One rule for every day | Ten parts | *Eight ways to live well
test: In religion lessons, how is the Eightfold Path often shown? | A square with four corners | A circle with no lines | *A wheel with eight spokes | A tall tower with five floors
test: Which phrase uses eightfold to mean eight times as much? | eight ways to live well | the Noble Eightfold Path | a wheel with eight spokes | *an eightfold rise
exam: Jess reads «The Noble Eightfold Path is eight ways to live well.» What does eightfold mean here? | Eight hundred years old | Lost in the woods | Eight times as much | *Having eight parts
